C linkage for membarrier (plan step R1.3): sys/membarrier.h is the one musl header that declares a function without
the extern "C" guards the others carry, as musl's master still is in 2026-10, so C++ code that calls membarrier
references a mangled name libc.so does not define. The runtime's GC takes its process-wide barrier from this header on
witos (R1.2b). The guards are spelled as in sys/mman.h; the change belongs upstream.

--- a/include/sys/membarrier.h
+++ b/include/sys/membarrier.h
@@ -16,6 +16,14 @@
 
 #define MEMBARRIER_CMD_FLAG_CPU 1
 
+#ifdef __cplusplus
+extern "C" {
+#endif
+
 int membarrier(int, int);
 
+#ifdef __cplusplus
+}
 #endif
+
+#endif
